 "text": "Hey, how's your day been so far? A six year old needs about half as much as a grow up, so around twenty to twenty five grams of protein per day. Yellow foods are great, things like sweetcorn, sweet potato, banana, oats and soy milk. But she needs lots of other things too. Coffee is fine, but a small slice of whole grain toast with peanut butter is easier on the tummy. That's a great idea. A family dinner where everyone gets to touch food before it gets on her plate is a big help.",
